      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a very sharp philosophical observation, often described as nihilism, which suggests that without an external universe, our choices really do seem like they carry no objective weight. However, many philosophers argue that even in an absurd universe, creating our *own* internal reasons is the ultimate rebellion and what gives our actions their specific meaning. Additionally, if staying or going feels equally pointless, then perhaps the \"point\" isn't about a grand destination, but simply about the quality of the journey right now, regardless of the outcome. This realization can shift the view from a cold zero-sum game to a personal canvas where you are the only artist deciding what matters.",
